From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: airoha: attach the PHY only once

phylink_of_phy_connect() was called from airoha_dev_open(), so the PHY was
re-attached on every "ip link set up" - netifd opens the port once during
boot and again when the interface is added to the bridge.  Each attach
runs phy_attach_direct() -> phy_init_hw() -> config_init(), re-initialising
the EN8811H; the copper link that was up (pcs_get_state link=1 at 12.8 s)
dropped right after the second attach (link=0 at 25.6 s), together with a
"Led ... renamed ... due to name collision" message that confirms the
double registration.

Track it with a per-port flag and connect only once.

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-10 19:03:16.199963822 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-10 19:03:16.199963822 +0800
@@ -1912,11 +1912,27 @@
 		dev->dev.of_node);
 
 	if (airhoa_is_phy_external(port)) {
-		err = phylink_of_phy_connect(port->phylink, dev->dev.of_node, 0);
-		if (err) {
-			netdev_err(dev, "%s: could not attach PHY: %d\n", __func__,
-				   err);
-			return err;
+		/* Attach the PHY only once.  phylink_of_phy_connect() ->
+		 * phy_attach_direct() -> phy_init_hw() -> config_init()
+		 * re-initialises the EN8811H; doing that on every dev_open()
+		 * (netifd opens the port once at boot and again when the
+		 * interface is added to the bridge) drops the copper link:
+		 *
+		 *   [12.8] lan1: PHY [..] driver [Airoha EN8811H] ; link=1
+		 *   [25.6] lan1: PHY [..] driver [Airoha EN8811H] ; link=0
+		 *
+		 * with a "Led ... renamed ... due to name collision" message
+		 * confirming the second attach.
+		 */
+		if (!port->phy_connected) {
+			err = phylink_of_phy_connect(port->phylink,
+						     dev->dev.of_node, 0);
+			if (err) {
+				netdev_err(dev, "%s: could not attach PHY: %d\n",
+					   __func__, err);
+				return err;
+			}
+			port->phy_connected = true;
 		}
 
 		phylink_start(port->phylink);
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h	2026-10-10 19:03:16.199963822 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h	2026-10-10 19:03:16.199963822 +0800
@@ -621,6 +621,12 @@
 	u64 fwd_tx_packets;
 
 	struct metadata_dst *dsa_meta[AIROHA_MAX_DSA_PORTS];
+
+	/* phylink_of_phy_connect() must run exactly once per port: doing it
+	 * in airoha_dev_open() re-initialises the PHY on every "ip link set
+	 * up" and drops the copper link of the EN8811H (link goes 1 -> 0).
+	 */
+	bool phy_connected;
 };
 
 #define AIROHA_RXD4_PPE_CPU_REASON	GENMASK(20, 16)
